 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "초대하기: Would you like to...? / Do you want to...? / I'd love to",
   "en": "invitations: Would you like to...?, I'd love to and polite excuses"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "초대할 때는 Would you like to + 동사원형 ...? 또는 Do you want to ...?를 씁니다. 수락은 I'd love to. / Yes, please., 거절은 I'm sorry, but I can't.처럼 이유를 덧붙이면 정중합니다. 대안은 How about + 명사 / -ing?로 제안합니다.",
   "en": "Invite with Would you like to + base verb ...? or Do you want to ...? Accept with I'd love to; refuse politely with I'm sorry, but I can't and give a reason. Suggest an alternative with How about + noun / -ing?"
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "초대 / inviting",
     "Would you like to have dinner with me?"
    ],
    [
     "수락 / accepting",
     "I'd love to come."
    ],
    [
     "거절 / refusing",
     "I'm sorry, I'm busy on Saturday."
    ],
    [
     "대안 / alternative",
     "How about Sunday instead?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "초대는 Would you like to ...?, 수락은 I'd love to.",
    "en": "Invite with Would you like to ...?; accept with I'd love to."
   },
   {
    "ko": "거절할 때는 I'm sorry + 이유.",
    "en": "When you refuse say I'm sorry + a reason."
   },
   {
    "ko": "How about 뒤에는 명사 또는 -ing.",
    "en": "After How about use a noun or -ing."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
